<p><strong>ChatGPT Ads are now available to self-service advertisers in India through OpenAI Ads Manager Beta.</strong> That makes 2026 an important testing year for Indian businesses, but it does not make the channel an automatic replacement for Google Ads, Meta Ads or SEO.</p>
<p>This article is the pillar page in Mega Techzy's ChatGPT Ads series. If you are ready to move from overview to execution, read <a href="/blog/how-to-advertise-on-chatgpt">how to advertise on ChatGPT step by step</a>. For planning, use our <a href="/blog/chatgpt-ads-cost-india">ChatGPT Ads cost guide for India</a>.</p>

<h2>What are ChatGPT Ads?</h2>
<p>ChatGPT Ads are paid placements shown separately from ChatGPT's answer. OpenAI says ads can appear below the end of a response, carry a sponsored label and do not influence the answer itself. During the current beta, ads may appear to eligible users on Free and Go plans, while Plus, Pro, Business, Enterprise and Edu accounts remain ad-free.</p>
<p>For advertisers, campaign creation and management happen in Ads Manager Beta. The platform supports campaign objectives, budgets, dates, country targeting, ad groups, context hints, creative, landing pages, review and performance reporting.</p>

<h2>Is ChatGPT Ads available in India?</h2>
<p>Yes. OpenAI's current <a href="https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001245-ads-manager-availability">Ads Manager availability list</a> marks India as available for self-service access. Availability and features can change during the beta, so advertisers should confirm the current country list and account options before finalising a launch plan.</p>
<p>India availability is different from guaranteed delivery. An advertiser still needs a verified account, a valid billing setup, approved ads, an active campaign and enough eligible inventory for delivery.</p>

<h2>Where and how can an ad appear?</h2>
<p>An ad can appear below a ChatGPT response and is visually separated from the answer. The creative can include an advertiser identity, title, copy, image and landing page. The placement matters because the user may be exploring a need, comparing options or narrowing a decision rather than typing a short commercial keyword.</p>
<p>OpenAI explains that delivery can consider the context and intent of the current conversation, the landing page, ad title, copy, advertiser-provided context hints and permitted personalization signals. Context hints are not exact-match keywords and do not guarantee an ad will appear in a particular conversation.</p>

<h2>Does advertising change ChatGPT answers?</h2>
<p>No. OpenAI states that ads run on separate systems and advertisers cannot shape, rank or alter ChatGPT responses. It also says advertisers do not receive users' chats, chat history, memories or personal details. Advertisers receive aggregated, non-identifying performance information such as views and clicks.</p>
<p>These boundaries are important for both users and brands. A sponsored placement is not an endorsement, and a responsible advertiser should never write creative that implies ChatGPT recommended the product.</p>

<h2>How are ChatGPT Ads priced?</h2>
<p>Ads Manager currently supports CPM, CPC and conversion-optimized CPC objectives. CPM is designed for reach and charges per 1,000 impressions. CPC is designed for traffic and charges per valid click. oCPC also charges per valid click but optimizes delivery toward a selected conversion event when measurement is configured.</p>
<p>There is no universal India-wide price that applies to every advertiser. OpenAI describes ChatGPT Ads as an early platform without broad performance benchmarks across industries or campaign types. Use the official platform guidance, then judge the channel through your own conversion quality and customer economics.</p>

<h2>What can advertisers measure?</h2>
<p>Ads Manager Beta reports impressions, clicks, spend, click-through rate, average CPC, average CPM and conversions when conversion measurement is configured. Advertisers can also add static UTM parameters to landing-page URLs so visits can be analysed in their existing analytics tools.</p>
<p>A useful reporting view connects ad-platform data with landing-page conversion rate, lead quality, sales outcome and customer acquisition cost. A low-cost click is not valuable if it creates no relevant enquiry.</p>

<h2>Good first use cases for Indian businesses</h2>
<ul>
    <li>A focused service offer that solves a clear research or comparison need.</li>
    <li>A product with a strong explanatory landing page and reliable conversion tracking.</li>
    <li>A high-consideration offer where context can help identify relevant conversations.</li>
    <li>A controlled awareness test for a brand that can measure incremental reach.</li>
</ul>
<p>Avoid advertising a long list of unrelated services in one ad. A specific offer such as an SEO and AI-search visibility audit is easier to explain and measure than a generic claim that an agency does everything.</p>

<h2>A practical first-test framework</h2>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Choose one outcome.</strong> Decide whether the test is for reach, qualified traffic or a tracked conversion.</li>
    <li><strong>Choose one offer.</strong> Match the ad, landing page and conversion action to the same customer need.</li>
    <li><strong>Build themed ad groups.</strong> Use context hints that describe relevant conversations without treating them as guaranteed keywords.</li>
    <li><strong>Create variations.</strong> Test distinct benefits and customer problems rather than tiny wording changes.</li>
    <li><strong>Measure the full path.</strong> Confirm forms, calls, analytics and sales feedback before increasing spend.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Advantages and limitations</h2>
<p>The opportunity is a new context-rich environment where people may be learning and comparing. The limitations are equally real: the product is in beta, availability and formats can evolve, broad benchmarks are limited and performance will differ by offer, creative, relevance and landing-page quality.</p>
<p>For a channel-by-channel decision, compare <a href="/blog/chatgpt-ads-vs-google-ads-meta-ads">ChatGPT Ads vs Google Ads vs Meta Ads</a>. Small teams should also read our guide to whether <a href="/blog/chatgpt-ads-small-business">ChatGPT Ads are worth testing for a small business</a>.</p>

<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>Can Indian businesses sign up directly?</h3>
<p>India is currently listed as available for self-service Ads Manager access. Account verification, billing and ad review still apply.</p>
<h3>Can advertisers read ChatGPT conversations?</h3>
<p>No. OpenAI says advertisers do not receive chats, chat history, memories or personal details.</p>
<h3>Are ChatGPT Ads better than Google Ads?</h3>
<p>Not automatically. The channels reach people in different environments. The better choice depends on the customer's mindset, the offer, measurement quality and commercial results.</p>

